content:
We need to build complete retrosynthesis route JSON for target molecule. We have data: template_search-1 gave mapped_rxn and template_id 84231 for SN2 step. apply_template-1 gave precursors list: ["COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nnn(Cc3ccc(CCl)cc3)c2N)c1", "C[NH+]4CC(F)C4"].

template_search-2 failed. template_search-3 failed. apply_template-2 and 3 both give same precursors list (maybe duplicate). So we have only one successful step: SN2 disconnection of a C-Cl to C-N? Actually mapped_rxn shows product with CCl replaced by C[NH+]4CC(F)C4? Wait mapped_rxn: COc1...CCl -> COc1...C[NH+]4CC(F)C4. So the target molecule (product) is with C[NH+]4CC(F)C4 (a quaternary ammonium?) Actually the product is the one with the cationic side chain. The precursor is the same aromatic core with CCl (chloride) and the nucleophile C[NH+]4CC(F)C4 (maybe a tertiary amine). So retrosynthesis: target -> precursors: aromatic chloride + amine.

Thus route JSON: root is target molecule (type mol, smiles target). children: reaction node with template_id 84231, children: two mol nodes for precursors.

We need target SMILES. Which is the product from mapped_rxn right side: "COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nnn(Cc3ccc(C[NH+]4CC(F)C4)cc3)c2N)c1". That's the target.

Thus JSON:

{
 "type":"mol",
 "smiles":"COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nnn(Cc3ccc(C[NH+]4CC(F)C4)cc3)c2N)c1",
 "children":[
   {
     "type":"reaction",
     "template_id":84231,
     "children":[
       {"type":"mol","smiles":"COc1cccc(NC(=O)c2nnn(Cc3ccc(CCl)cc3)c2N)c1"},
       {"type":"mol","smiles":"C[NH+]4CC(F)C4"}
     ]
   }
 ]
}

We should verify route using verify_route tool. Let's do that.
